New: FESubfaceValues and hp::FESubfaceValues accept an hp::QCollection
with one face quadrature for each face of the reference cell, as
FEFaceValues already does. This makes subfaces of wedges and pyramids
possible, whose faces are triangles and quadrilaterals. FEInterfaceValues
has a new constructor that takes one such collection for each finite
element; each side of a face then uses the quadrature of its own element,
so that hanging faces between cells of different shapes are supported.
<br>
(Lukas Dreyer, 2026/11/26)
